<title>INDIA: India's SEBI approves 3 foreign debt funds.</title>
<headline>India's SEBI approves 3 foreign debt funds.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) on Thursday cleared three foreign debt funds worth $253 million, Chairman D.R. Mehta said.</p>
<p>The three funds are J. Henry Schroeder, Credit-Suisse and Chescor, SEBI senior executive director Pratip Kar said.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
